      VFMV_V_F and VFMERGE_VFM use FPR32 register class for their scalar FP operand (rs1). This is architecturally correct: Zdinx is a scalar FP-in-GPR extension and does not affect V-extension vector FP instructions. Vector FP instructions with scalar operands always source the scalar from the FP register file, never from GPRs. The spec's concern about 'reading only a single x-register on RV32+Zdinx for EEW=64' applies only if an INX variant of these instructions existed — none is defined here. The FPR32 operand class ensures the scalar value comes from an FP register, not an x-register, making sign-extension truncation impossible.
  [OK] contrib/llvm-project/llvm/lib/Target/RISCV/RISCVInstrInfoV.td:1692-1694  (TableGen record: VFMV_S_F)
      VFMV_S_F (vfmv.s.f) uses FPR32 register class for its scalar FP operand (rs1), identical pattern to VFMV_V_F. This is the 'scalar-to-vector-element-0' counterpart. Same architectural reasoning: vector FP instructions are not affected by Zdinx; they always use FPRs for scalar operands. No INX variant exists, so the Zdinx register-pair concern does not apply.
