      ZdinxExt (RV64) maps f64 scalar FP operands to FPR64INX (a single GPR). Zdinx32Ext (RV32) maps f64 to FPR64IN32X (a GPRPair). Both are scoped to scalar D-extension instructions via ExtInfo and are guarded by Predicates=[HasStdExtZdinx, IsRV64] or [HasStdExtZdinx, IsRV32]. The RV32 case correctly requires GPRPair for 64-bit values where XLEN=32. These ExtInfo records are only used for scalar D instructions (FLD, FSD, FADD.D, etc.) — they are never referenced by V-extension definitions. No cross-contamination with vector FP instructions.Wrote 3 report(s) → output/riscv-isa-manual/pr-2419/

